# Lease requests

What a worker sends to take work and to keep it: flat records with derived codecs,
read CLOSED, so a field the coordinator does not know is refused, never ignored,
and a worker built against another contract finds out on its first request.

## Note
A worker asking for a unit. `holder` is the contributor's id; `kinds` narrows the
unit kinds it takes, comma-separated, empty for every kind a worker may lease;
`focus` narrows the problems to a cohort, collection, category or problem id,
empty for anywhere; `ttlMs` asks for a lease length, zero for the default; and
`budgetMicros` is what the contributor set aside, shown on the leaderboard.

## A LeaseRequest has:
    a holder, which is Text.
    a displayName, which is Text.
    a kinds, which is Text.
    a focus, which is Text.
    a ttlMs, which is Int.
    a budgetMicros, which is Int.

## Note
A worker still on its unit, asking for its lease to run on, with the lease's secret.
## A HeartbeatRequest has:
    a unitId, which is Text.
    a token, which is Int.
    a holder, which is Text.
    a secret, which is Text.
    a ttlMs, which is Int.

## Note
The unit kinds a worker may lease: all but `verify`, which only the trusted
verifier takes, from the database, so no worker can verify its own claim.

## To leasableKinds () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["formalize", "review", "prove", "decompose", "special_case", "counterexample", "repair", "summarize_trail", "link", "improve_strategy"].

## Note
The kinds a request names, or every leasable kind when it names none.
## To requestedKinds (kinds: Text) -> Seq of Text:
    If trim(kinds) is equal to "":
        Return leasableKinds().
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for k in split(kinds, ","):
        Push trim(k) to out.
    Return out.

## Note
Whether a contributor id has the schema's shape: 1 to 80 of `A-Za-z0-9_.:-`.
## To isHolderId (t: Text) -> Bool:
    If length of t is equal to 0 or length of t is greater than 80:
        Return false.
    Repeat for b in text_bytes(t):
        Let letter be (b is at least 97 and b is at most 122) or (b is at least 65 and b is at most 90).
        If (letter or (b is at least 45 and b is at most 58) or b is equal to 95) is equal to false or b is equal to 47:
            Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
The first thing wrong with a lease request, or the empty text when nothing is.
## To leaseRequestProblem (r: LeaseRequest) -> Text:
    If isHolderId(r's holder) is equal to false:
        Return "holder must be 1 to 80 of A-Za-z0-9_.:-".
    If length of r's displayName is greater than 120 or length of r's focus is greater than 200:
        Return "displayName is at most 120 bytes and focus at most 200".
    If r's budgetMicros is less than 0 or r's ttlMs is less than 0:
        Return "budgetMicros and ttlMs cannot be negative".
    Let mutable seen be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for k in requestedKinds(r's kinds):
        If leasableKinds() contains k is equal to false or seen contains k:
            Return "kind \"{k}\" is not one a worker may lease, or is repeated".
        Push k to seen.
    Return "".

## Note
A JSON object body, refused when it carries a key not in `keys`.
## To closedBody (body: Text, keys: Seq of Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect jsonParseStrict(body):
        When JErr (m):
            Return a new Err with error "not JSON: " + m.
        When JOk (v):
            Inspect jsonNoExtraKeys(v, keys):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error e.
                When Ok (fine):
                    Return a new Ok with value body.
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable body".

## Test: coordinator lease requests are closed records

Let body be toJson_LeaseRequest(a new LeaseRequest with holder "ada-1" and displayName "Ada" and kinds "prove,repair" and focus "erdos" and ttlMs 0 and budgetMicros 5000000).
Inspect closedBody(body, ["holder", "displayName", "kinds", "focus", "ttlMs", "budgetMicros"]):
    When Ok (b):
        Expect that b is equal to body.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "closed".
Inspect closedBody("{{\"holder\":\"a\",\"extra\":1}}", ["holder"]):
    When Ok (b):
        Expect that b is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "unexpected key \"extra\"".

## Test: coordinator lease rules name what is wrong

Let good be a new LeaseRequest with holder "ada-1" and displayName "Ada" and kinds "" and focus "" and ttlMs 0 and budgetMicros 0.
Expect that leaseRequestProblem(good) is equal to "".
Expect that requestedKinds("prove, repair") is equal to ["prove", "repair"].
Expect that length of requestedKinds("") is equal to 10.
Expect that leaseRequestProblem(a new LeaseRequest with holder "a/b" and displayName "" and kinds "" and focus "" and ttlMs 0 and budgetMicros 0) contains "holder".
Expect that leaseRequestProblem(a new LeaseRequest with holder "a" and displayName "" and kinds "verify" and focus "" and ttlMs 0 and budgetMicros 0) contains "verify".

## Test: coordinator workers never lease verification

Expect that leasableKinds() contains "verify" is equal to false.
For all booleans asksVerify:
    Let mutable kinds be "prove".
    If asksVerify:
        Set kinds to "prove,verify".
    Let r be a new LeaseRequest with holder "w" and displayName "" and kinds kinds and focus "" and ttlMs 0 and budgetMicros 0.
    Expect that (leaseRequestProblem(r) is equal to "") is equal to (asksVerify is equal to false).
